From: tao3k team and Contributors
Subject: [PATCH] std/make: expose Darwin module-index progress at verbose level 3

The first worker cannot announce a compile until std/make has imported every
build-spec module to derive its completion identity. On a large Darwin package,
this legitimate macro-expansion phase can exceed the consumer's 10-second
silence watchdog. Report real indexed-module progress through std/make's
existing flushed message path. Keep the official import and graph algorithm,
non-Darwin behavior, and non-verbose output unchanged.
---
 src/std/make.ss | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/std/make.ss b/src/std/make.ss
--- a/src/std/make.ss
+++ b/src/std/make.ss
@@ -339,12 +339,26 @@
     ;; prepare the build
     (create-directory* (settings-bindir settings))
     (create-directory* (settings-libdir settings))
     (create-directory* (path-expand "static" (settings-libdir settings)))
 
     ;; prepare the completion table
-    (for (spec buildspec)
-      (let (id (module-id spec))
-        (hash-put! completions id (make-completion `(build ,id)))))
+    (let ((progress?
+           (and (settings-verbose>=? settings 3)
+                (cond-expand (darwin #t) (else #f))))
+          (indexed 0))
+      (when progress?
+        (message "... build-observe phase=module-index event=start total="
+                 (length buildspec)))
+      (for (spec buildspec)
+        (let (id (module-id spec))
+          (hash-put! completions id (make-completion `(build ,id))))
+        (set! indexed (+ indexed 1))
+        (when (and progress? (zero? (modulo indexed 16)))
+          (message "... build-observe phase=module-index event=progress indexed="
+                   indexed)))
+      (when progress?
+        (message "... build-observe phase=module-index event=end indexed="
+                 indexed)))
 
     ;; spawn a thread for each spec that waits for the dependency completions
     ;; and pushes to the work channel if necessary.
